# Android Interactive Architecture Flow Documentation

## 1. Objective & Strict Scope

Analyze a real Android repository and generate a **static, interactive HTML/web documentation site** that visualizes the application's architecture, execution flows, component interactions, and data transformations.

### Included in Scope
- Architecture components across all inferred project layers.
- Complete execution chains from real entry points (UI or background) to terminal exit points (APIs, databases, local storage, SDKs, workers, notifications, or another flow).
- Directed relationships between classes, interfaces, objects, and external dependencies.
- Method calls, signatures, parameters, parameter types, and return types.
- Data transferred and explicit data transformations (`Intent/NavArgs -> Request -> DTO -> Entity -> DomainModel -> UiState`).
- Communication mechanisms (`Direct call`, `Suspend function`, `StateFlow`, `SharedFlow`, `Flow`, `LiveData`, `Callback`, `Intent / Bundle`, `Navigation Args`, `Hilt / Dagger DI`, `EventBus / Observer`, `WorkManager`, `Retrofit HTTP`, `Room SQL`, `SDK Bridge`, `Reflection / Dynamic`).
- Synchronous vs. asynchronous execution flags.
- Line-numbered source code traceability (`file`, `symbol`, `line`, relevant snippet).

### Excluded (Do NOT Generate)
- Architecture compliance audits or Clean Architecture policing.
- Code quality, performance, security, or technical debt scoring.
- Refactoring recommendations or coding convention enforcement.
- Unit test coverage reports or invented health/innovation metrics.

