## 4. 7-Phase Execution Workflow

### Phase 1 — Project Discovery
1. Inspect `settings.gradle(.kts)`, `build.gradle(.kts)`, and `AndroidManifest.xml` to map Gradle modules (`:app`, `:feature:*`, `:domain:*`, `:data:*`, `:core:*`, `:legacy:*`).
2. Scan Kotlin and Java source files for Activities, Fragments, `@Composable` screens, `ViewModel` subclasses, UseCases/Interactors, Repositories, DataSources, Retrofit/Ktor APIs, Room `@Database`/`@Dao`, DataStore, Managers, Controllers, Observers, Workers, Services, and SDK wrappers.
3. Map DI bindings (`@HiltViewModel`, `@Module`, `@Binds`, `@Provides`, Koin modules, manual factories).

### Phase 2 — Entry Point Discovery
Identify real entry points per flow:
- `MAIN` / `LAUNCHER` Activity.
- Deep-link `intent-filter` Activities (`app://...`).
- Compose `NavHost` routes & Fragment destinations.
- Background `FirebaseMessagingService`, `Service`, `BroadcastReceiver`, and `CoroutineWorker`.

### Phase 3 — Flow Reconstruction
For each flow:
1. Start at its entry point (`isEntryPoint: true`).
2. Trace every invocation, reactive collection, DI binding, navigation action, and event publication until terminal exit points (`isExitPoint: true`: Backend API, Room SQLite, DataStore/SharedPreferences, External SDK, OS NotificationManager, or WorkManager).
3. Consolidate multiple calls between the same `(source, target)` pair into one `FlowEdge` with multiple entries inside `calls[]`.

### Phase 4 — Data Flow & Transformation Analysis
1. Document input parameters, return types, sync vs. async, and communication mechanism per call.
2. Track every model transformation (`Intent`, `Bundle`, `NavArgs`, `Request`, `DTO`, `Entity`, `Domain`, `UiState`, `Event`) and store the ordered chain in `flow.transformationPipeline`.

### Phase 5 — Graph & Data Model Generation
Generate the decoupled JSON model (`project.json`, `flows.json`, `components.json`, `flows/<flow-id>.json`):
- Populate structured class members per node (`constructorParams`, `properties`, `publicMethods`, `privateMethods`, `calledByOthers`, `callingOthers`, `dataReceived`, `dataEmitted`) and concise `classSnippet`.
- Assign clean non-overlapping layer coordinates left-to-right (`Presentation` -> `Domain` -> `Data` -> `Network` [top] / `Local Storage` [bottom] -> `External`) so edges route cleanly without crossing unrelated layers.

### Phase 6 — Static Interactive Web Explorer Generation
Build a static, offline-ready web application (no backend server required; bundle dependencies locally or via static build).

